.\" tvmail-backend(1) man page.
.TH TVMAIL\-BACKEND 1 "September 2026" "tvmail 1.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
tvmail\-backend \- the part of tvmail that does the actual work
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B tvmail\-backend
.I subcommand
.RI [ args ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B tvmail\-backend
is a small, standard\-library\-only Python program that performs every
mail\-format operation on behalf of
.BR tvmail (1):
listing mailboxes, decoding MIME, composing message skeletons, handing outgoing
mail to
.BR sendmail (8),
deleting, marking, saving drafts, and expanding
.I ~/.mailrc
aliases.
.PP
.BR tvmail (1)
runs it as a child process and reads its output.
It is documented \(em and packaged \(em separately because it is perfectly
usable on its own from a shell or a script; the Turbo Vision front end holds no
mail logic that this does not.
.PP
Each subcommand prints its result to standard output and exits
.B 0
on success,
.B 1
on a usage or not\-found error, or
.B 2
on a runtime failure.
.SH "MAILBOX ARGUMENT"
Wherever a subcommand takes a
.I MBOX
argument it accepts either a filesystem path or one of these shorthands:
.TP
.B spool
.I $MAIL
or
.IR /var/mail/$USER .
.TP
.B mbox
.IR ~/mbox .
.TP
.B drafts
.IR $folder/drafts
(default
.IR ~/Mail/drafts ),
where
.I $folder
is
.B "set folder"
from the mailrc files.
.TP
.B trash
.IR ~/.local/share/tvmail/trash.mbox .
.TP
.B dead
.I $DEAD
or
.IR ~/dead.letter ,
treated as a single\-message mailbox.
.SH SUBCOMMANDS
.TP
.BI "list " [MBOX]
One line per message:
.IR "index" ,
tab,
.I flags
.RB ( N
new or
.B .
seen), tab,
.IR date ,
tab,
.IR from ,
tab,
.IR subject .
A mailbox that does not exist yet lists as empty.
.TP
.BI "show " "IDX " [MBOX]
Decoded headers followed by the best available text of message
.IR IDX .
.TP
.BI "raw " "IDX " [MBOX]
The message exactly as stored.
.TP
.BI "parts " "IDX " [MBOX]
One line per MIME part:
.IR "part\-number" ,
.IR content\-type ,
.IR filename ,
.IR bytes .
.TP
.BI "save " "IDX PARTNO DEST " [MBOX]
Write the decoded payload of one MIME part to
.IR DEST .
.TP
.BI "delete " "IDX " "\fR[\fPIDX ...\fR]\fP " "\fR[\fP--mbox " "MBOX\fR]\fP " "\fR[\fP--trash " "DEST\fR]\fP"
Remove one or more messages.
With
.BR \-\-trash ,
each is appended to
.I DEST
first.
A
.I .bak
of the mailbox is kept.
.TP
.BI "mark " "IDX " "read|unread " [MBOX]
Set or clear the Status flag.
.TP
.BI "compose\-template " "\fR[\fP--to " "A\fR]\fP " "\fR[\fP--subject " "S\fR]\fP " "\fR[\fP--in-reply-to " "IDX\fR]\fP " [MBOX]
Print a draft skeleton: a
.BR From: ,
.BR To: ,
.B Subject:
block, a blank line, and (for a reply) the quoted original.
.TP
.BI "send " "\fR[\fP--from " "A\fR]\fP " "\fR[\fP--to " "A ...\fR]\fP " "\fR[\fP--subject " "S\fR]\fP"
Read an RFC\ 822 message (or a bare body, with
.BR \-\-to )
on standard input and hand it to
.BR sendmail (8).
.B alias
and
.B group
names in
.BR To: ,
.B Cc:
and
.B Bcc:
are expanded from the mailrc files before delivery.
.TP
.B save\-draft
Read an RFC\ 822 message on standard input and append it to the
.B drafts
mailbox, adding a
.B Date:
header if absent.
.TP
.B aliases
Print the address book:
.I name
tab
.IR "expanded, addresses" ,
one per line.
.TP
.B pull
Run
.B pop\-pull
if it is on
.IR PATH .
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /etc/mailrc ", " ~/.mailrc
Read for
.BR "set folder" ,
.BR "set DEAD" ,
and
.BR alias / group .
.TP
.I /usr/sbin/sendmail
The delivery agent used by
.BR send .
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.B MAIL ", " DEAD ", " MAILRC
override the corresponding defaults.
